label a0525:
    # --- Day 11: 2025-05-25 ---
    scene bg bedroom
    $ show_calendar()
    show mood_home zorder 3
    with dissolve_scene_full
    play music dailyleisure
    window auto
    "Sunday wakes me up one minute before the first alarm."
    "Not fifteen minutes after, not in the middle of a dream where my phone has become an accusing rectangle."
    "One minute before."
    "{i}Look at that. Personal growth, or fear with better timing.{/i}"
    "The screen reads 7:14."
    "My first alarm waits at 7:15, smug and unemployed."
    "I turn it off before it can develop a personality."
    "The other three alarms sit beneath it like backup prosecutors."
    "I disable those too."
    "{i}Saturday earned me caution. Sunday is apparently getting the benefits.{/i}"
    "For a few seconds, I stay under the blanket and listen."
    "The house is quiet."
    "Not empty quiet -- weekend quiet."
    "Pipes settling, the faint hum of the refrigerator downstairs, somebody's car passing on the street with no interest in my academic future."
    "My bag is already packed beside the desk."
    "Algebra sheet, civics notes, literature handouts, science review, English vocabulary."
    "A whole weekend reduced to paper with corners."
    "{i}Library at nine.{/i}"
    "{i}Second-floor windows.{/i}"
    "{i}Monika and emotional stability, allegedly.{/i}"
    "The thought does something annoying to my chest."
    "Not bad, just noticeable."
    "I sit up before the room can ask for clarification."
    $ hide_calendar()
    scene black with wipeleft_scene
    nier "Morning gets handled in pieces."
    nier "Shower, clothes, transit card, wallet, the review sheets I checked twice last night and still check again because anxiety enjoys clerical work."
    nier "Downstairs, the kitchen has tea in the pot, a note from Mom, and no sign of Asahina, which means she is either asleep or pretending Sunday morning has no jurisdiction over her."
    call nier_clear from _call_nier_clear_0525_1
    scene bg kitchen
    $ show_calendar()
    show mood_home zorder 3
    with wipeleft_scene
    "The note is stuck to the counter beside a covered plate."
    "{i}Breakfast. Text when you arrive. Do not live on pastries. - Mom{/i}"
    "The plate contains rice, egg, and the exact amount of parental awareness required to make ignoring it feel legally dangerous."
    "I eat."
    "This is less a moral victory than compliance with a very small court order."
    "My phone buzzes before I finish."
    python:
        _phone_messages = [
            phone_msg("them", "Morning. Are you awake?"),
            phone_msg("me", "Before the alarm, somehow."),
            phone_msg("them", "That is either impressive or concerning."),
            phone_msg("me", "Both can be true."),
            phone_msg("them", "I am leaving in a few minutes. Same table as planned."),
            phone_msg("me", "Second-floor windows, right?"),
            phone_msg("them", "Yep. I brought flashcards and a terrifying amount of sticky notes."),
            phone_msg("me", "Define terrifying."),
            phone_msg("them", "You will know it when you see it."),
            phone_msg("me", "Comforting. I'll head out after breakfast."),
            phone_msg("them", "Eat real food."),
            phone_msg("me", "Did my mom brief you?"),
            phone_msg("them", "No, I simply understand you."),
            phone_msg("me", "Worse."),
        ]
